-- title:
--   Hyperbolic term of the twisted trace formula: affine or zero
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $K$ and $L$ are number fields with $L/K$ Galois, $\sigma$ is a $K$-automorphism of $L$, and the hypothesis `hgen` states that every $\tau \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$ (so the group is generated by $\sigma$). The descent datum $D$ is a record [`M4aHerbrand.IdeleGaloisDescent`](def/M4aHerbrand_IdeleClassVocab.html#L28) consisting of a homomorphism $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K) \to \operatorname{RingAut}(\mathbb{A}_L)$ that is compatible with the diagonal embedding of $L$ and acts continuously; write $\sigma_{\mathbb{A}}$ for the induced entrywise automorphism [`AutomorphicForm.sigmaAdelicAct K L D σ`](def/AutomorphicForm_SigmaAdelicAction.html#L14) of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ and $D.\mathrm{unitsAct}\,\sigma$ for the induced automorphism of $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$. Write $\iota$ for [`AutomorphicForm.globalPoints`](def/AutomorphicForm_AdelicLsXi.html#L15) (the entrywise map $\mathrm{GL}_2(L) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$), $c$ for [`AutomorphicForm.centralScalar`](def/AutomorphicForm_AdelicLsXi.html#L18) (the scalar-matrix map $\mathbb{A}_L^\times \to \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$), $n(s)$ for [`AutomorphicForm.unipotentGL2 s`](def/AutomorphicForm_ConstantTerm.html#L17) $= \begin{pmatrix}1&s\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$, $w$ for [`AutomorphicForm.adelicWeyl`](def/AutomorphicForm_WeylIntertwining.html#L35) (the image under $\iota$ of the antidiagonal involution $\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\1&0\end{pmatrix}$), $\mathrm{H}$ for [`NumberField.AdelicHeight.adelicHeight L`](def/NumberField_AdelicHeight.html#L158) (the product of the archimedean and finite adelic heights), and $\mu_{\mathrm{GL}}$ for the Haar measure `adelicGLHaar (Fin 2) (𝓞 L) L` on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ for its Borel structure.
--
--   The data and hypotheses are grouped as follows.
--
--   Determinant slab and central measure data: reals $\alpha, \beta$ with $0 < \alpha$ (`hα`) and $\alpha < \beta$ (`hαβ`); a Haar measure $\nu_Z$ on $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ for a measurable structure making it a Borel space; a set $\Omega_L \subseteq \mathbb{A}_L^\times$ which by `hΩL` is a fundamental domain for the range of $L^\times \to \mathbb{A}_L^\times$ acting on $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ with respect to $\nu_Z$.
--
--   Central character data: a homomorphism $\xi$ from the top subgroup of $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$, with `hξc` asserting that $z \mapsto \xi(z)$ is continuous as a $\mathbb{C}$-valued function and `hξt` asserting $\xi(z) = 1$ for $z$ in the range of $L^\times \to \mathbb{A}_L^\times$.
--
--   Fundamental-domain data in the slab: reals $c_0, u, d_1, d_2$ with $0 < c_0$ (`hc`), a compact set $T_c \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ (`hTc`), and a set $\Phi_0 \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ subject to three conditions: `hΦ₀S`, that $\Phi_0$ is contained in the union over $y \in T_c$ of the right translates by $y$ of the centre-cut Siegel set `WindowedSiegel.centreCutSiegelSet L c₀ u d₁ d₂` (finite part integral, all local heights $\geq c_0$, all window coordinates $\le u^2$, all archimedean determinant norms in $[d_1,d_2]$); `hΦ₀s`, that $\Phi_0$ lies in the slab $\{g : \|\det g\|_{\mathbb{A}_L} \in [\alpha,\beta]\}$, the idèle norm being the module [`NumberField.TateGlobal.ideleNorm`](def/NumberField_TateGlobalZeta.html#L19); and `hΦ₀`, that $\Phi_0$ is a fundamental domain for the range of $\iota$ acting on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ with respect to $\mu_{\mathrm{GL}}$ restricted to that slab.
--
--   Twisted centraliser data: a subgroup $H \leq \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$, closed (`hHc`), characterised by `hH`: $h \in H$ if and only if the $(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$ entries of $h$ vanish and $\sigma_{\mathbb{A}}(h)h^{-1}$ is central in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$; together with a right-invariant Haar measure $\mu_H$ on $H$. For $t \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ set $I(t) = \{\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L) \mid \exists g,\ t^{-1}\bigl(g^{-1}\delta\, \sigma(g)\bigr) \in Z(\mathrm{GL}_2(L))\}$, where $\sigma$ acts entrywise.
--
--   Transversal data: a set $\Delta \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ with `hΔd`, every $t \in \Delta$ has vanishing $(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$ entries and $N_{L/K}(t_{00}/t_{11}) \neq 1$; `hΔdisj`, the sets $I(t)$, $t \in \Delta$, are pairwise disjoint for distinct $t, t'$; and `hΔcov`, the set
--   $$S_\sigma = \{\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L) \mid \exists \gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K),\ \gamma \in \mathtt{hyperbolicCell}\ K,\ \mathtt{normClassMap}\ \mathtt{hgen}\,(\mathtt{SigmaConjClasses.mk}\ \sigma\ \delta) = \mathtt{ConjClasses.mk}\ \gamma\}$$
--   is contained in $\bigcup_{t \in \Delta} I(t)$; here [`AutomorphicForm.hyperbolicCell K`](def/AutomorphicForm_GL2ConjugacyCells.html#L32) is the set of $\gamma$ whose characteristic polynomial equals $(X-a)(X-b)$ with $a \neq b$ in $K$, and [`LT.TwistedNorm.normClassMap hgen`](def/TwistedNormClasses.html#L766) is the map sending a $\sigma$-twisted conjugacy class in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ to a conjugacy class in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$.
--
--   A set $\Phi_L \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ is also given; it occurs only as the carrier field of the record `productionPinsOf L ΦL (fun M => levelOne (𝓞 L) L M ⊓ finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup L) (fun w => heckeGen (𝓞 L) L w) (adelicBox L)`, of which the statement uses only the field `nS`, the Borel structure `adeleBorel` on $\mathbb{A}_L$, and the field `ν`, the additive Haar measure on $\mathbb{A}_L$ conditioned on the box `adelicBox L`.
--
--   Two abbreviations for the quantities occurring in the conclusion. First, for $t \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ and $y \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ put
--   $$F_t(y) \;=\; \int_{\mathbb{A}_L^\times} \xi(z)\, \varphi\bigl(y^{-1}\,\iota(t)\, \sigma_{\mathbb{A}}(c(z)\,y)\bigr)\, d\nu_Z(z).$$
--   Second, for $R \in \mathbb{R}$, $x \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ and $z \in \mathbb{A}_L^\times$ put
--   $$E_R(x,z) \;=\; \xi(z)\Bigl(\textstyle\sum^{\mathrm{f}}_{\delta \in S_\sigma} \varphi\bigl(x^{-1}\iota(\delta)\,\sigma_{\mathbb{A}}(c(z)x)\bigr) \;-\; \mathbf{1}_{\{g\,:\,\mathrm{H}(g) > e^{R}\}}(c(z)x)\cdot \mathrm{CT}_x(c(z)x)\Bigr),$$
--   where $\sum^{\mathrm{f}}$ denotes the finsum over the indicated subset, $\{g : \mathrm{H}(g) > e^R\}$ is [`AutomorphicForm.highSet`](def/AutomorphicForm_TruncationOperator.html#L36) for the adelic height at threshold $e^R$, and
--   $$\mathrm{CT}_x(g) \;=\; \int_{\mathbb{A}_L} \ \textstyle\sum^{\mathrm{f}}_{\delta \in J} \varphi\bigl(x^{-1}\iota(\delta)\,\sigma_{\mathbb{A}}(n(s)\,g)\bigr)\, d\nu_{\mathrm{box}}(s)$$
--   is the constant term [`AutomorphicForm.constantTerm`](def/AutomorphicForm_ConstantTerm.html#L47) taken with respect to the conditioned measure $\nu_{\mathrm{box}}$ described above, the unipotent family $s \mapsto n(s)$, and the index set $J = \{\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L) \mid \gamma_{10} = 0 \ \text{and}\ N_{L/K}(\gamma_{00}/\gamma_{11}) \neq 1\}$. The quotient $H \backslash \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ is the orbit quotient `MulAction.orbitRel.Quotient H (AdelicGL2 (𝓞 L) L)`, equipped with the measure [`HaarQuotient.measure`](def/HaarQuotient.html#L28) $\mu_{\mathrm{GL}}\,H\,\mu_H$, and $q.\mathrm{out}$ denotes a chosen representative of the class $q$.
--
--   The conclusion is the conjunction of two implications.
--
--   First implication: if $\xi(D.\mathrm{unitsAct}\,\sigma\,z) = \xi(z)$ for all $z \in \mathbb{A}_L^\times$, then there is a function $a : \mathrm{GL}_2(L) \to \mathbb{C}$ which is bounded, i.e. $\|a(t)\| \le C$ for all $t$ and some real $C$, such that for every $\varphi : \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L) \to \mathbb{C}$ satisfying [`AutomorphicForm.IsFactorizableTestFn L φ`](def/AutomorphicForm_FactorizableTestFn.html#L38) (that is, $\varphi(g) = f_\infty(g_\infty) f_{\mathrm{fin}}(g_{\mathrm{fin}})$ with $f_\infty$ of the form $\Phi \circ (\text{archimedean entries})$ for a smooth $\Phi$ and compactly supported, and $f_{\mathrm{fin}}$ locally constant and compactly supported) there is a finite subset $\Delta_\varphi$ of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ with $\Delta_\varphi \subseteq \Delta$ for which the following hold.
--
--   (i) For every $t \in \Delta$ with $t \notin \Delta_\varphi$ and every $y \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$, $F_t(y) = 0$.
--
--   (ii) For every $t \in \Delta_\varphi$, the function $q \mapsto F_t(q.\mathrm{out})$ is integrable on $H \backslash \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ for the quotient measure, and so is the function
--   $$q \mapsto \bigl(-\log \mathrm{H}(q.\mathrm{out}) - \log \mathrm{H}(w\,q.\mathrm{out})\bigr)\, F_t(q.\mathrm{out}),$$
--   the real weight being coerced to $\mathbb{C}$.
--
--   (iii) There is $R_0 \in \mathbb{R}$ such that for every $R \geq R_0$: for every $x$, the function $z \mapsto E_R(x,z)$ is integrable on $\Omega_L$ with respect to $\nu_Z$; the function $x \mapsto \int_{\Omega_L} E_R(x,z)\, d\nu_Z(z)$ is integrable on $\Phi_0$ with respect to $\mu_{\mathrm{GL}}$; and
--   $$\int_{\Phi_0} \int_{\Omega_L} E_R(x,z)\, d\nu_Z(z)\, d\mu_{\mathrm{GL}}(x) \;=\; R \sum_{t \in \Delta_\varphi} 2\,a(t) \int_{H \backslash \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)} F_t(q.\mathrm{out})\, dq \; + \; \sum_{t \in \Delta_\varphi} a(t) \int_{H \backslash \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)} \bigl(-\log \mathrm{H}(q.\mathrm{out}) - \log \mathrm{H}(w\,q.\mathrm{out})\bigr) F_t(q.\mathrm{out})\, dq,$$
--   both integrals over the quotient being taken with respect to the measure [`HaarQuotient.measure`](def/HaarQuotient.html#L28) $\mu_{\mathrm{GL}}\,H\,\mu_H$, and $R$ coerced to $\mathbb{C}$.
--
--   Second implication: if it is not the case that $\xi(D.\mathrm{unitsAct}\,\sigma\,z) = \xi(z)$ for all $z$, then for every factorizable test function $\varphi$ there is $R_0 \in \mathbb{R}$ such that for every $R \geq R_0$ the same two integrability assertions hold — $z \mapsto E_R(x,z)$ is integrable on $\Omega_L$ for $\nu_Z$ for each $x$, and $x \mapsto \int_{\Omega_L} E_R(x,z)\, d\nu_Z(z)$ is integrable on $\Phi_0$ for $\mu_{\mathrm{GL}}$ — and
--   $$\int_{\Phi_0} \int_{\Omega_L} E_R(x,z)\, d\nu_Z(z)\, d\mu_{\mathrm{GL}}(x) = 0.$$
--
--   Thus the truncated hyperbolic contribution is, for all large truncation parameters $R$, an affine function of $R$ whose slope is twice the sum of the twisted orbital integrals $\int F_t$ weighted by $a(t)$ and whose constant term is the corresponding sum of weighted twisted orbital integrals, unless the central character fails to be $\sigma$-invariant, in which case the contribution vanishes identically for large $R$.
--
--   This is the explicit form, for factorizable test functions, of the statement that the hyperbolic contribution to the geometric side of the twisted $\mathrm{GL}_2$ trace formula for a cyclic extension $L/K$ is a polynomial of degree one in the truncation parameter, with slope given by twisted orbital integrals over the twisted centraliser $H$ and constant term by the corresponding height-weighted orbital integrals, together with the dichotomy that the whole contribution vanishes when the central character is not $\sigma$-invariant. It is used by the results that extract the affine shape of the hyperbolic term in bare form, that bound the two coefficients, and that assemble the winding datum comparison from that affine shape.
